{
  "group": "payload",
  "upstream": "engine.io-parser@5.2.3",
  "note": "encodePayload / decodePayload: the HTTP long-polling batch, in which several packets share one body joined by the Engine.IO v4 record separator U+001E (written \\u001e in these cases). Binary payloads are lowercase hex in the case specs and always travel base64 (\"b\"-prefixed) inside a payload, never as raw bytes. A payload with any unparseable member must fail as a whole on both sides. `eio.roundTrip` encodes a batch and decodes it again, returning both the wire string and the recovered packets.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "encpay-single",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "hello"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "a one-packet payload carries no separator"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-two-messages",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "b"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-empty-batch",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": []
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "no packets encodes to the empty string in the port; upstream never calls back at all",
      "deviation": "engine.io-parser's encodePayload counts completed packets against the batch length, so for an EMPTY batch the counter never reaches the length and the callback is NEVER invoked — upstream simply hangs. engineio.EncodePayload returns the empty string. Upstream is the outlier (a latent hang); the port is not going to reproduce it."
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-all-types",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "open",
              "data": "{\"sid\":\"x\"}"
            },
            {
              "type": "close"
            },
            {
              "type": "ping",
              "data": "probe"
            },
            {
              "type": "pong",
              "data": "probe"
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "hi"
            },
            {
              "type": "upgrade"
            },
            {
              "type": "noop"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "all seven packet types in one batch"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-empty-data-packets",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "two empty MESSAGEs are distinguishable from one, because the type prefix survives"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-binary-only",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "binary": "00ff10"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "inside a payload binary is always base64: \"b\" + base64(00 ff 10)"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-binary-mixed",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "text"
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "binary": "0102"
            },
            {
              "type": "ping"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-binary-with-separator-byte",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "binary": "1e1e"
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "after"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "base64 is exactly why the separator byte inside binary data cannot split the batch"
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-data-contains-separator",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "a\u001eb"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload",
      "note": "the format has no escaping: a text payload containing the separator is emitted verbatim by both implementations and will decode as two packets. Recorded, not fixed — changing it would break the wire format."
    },
    {
      "id": "encpay-unicode",
      "fn": "eio.encodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "packets": [
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "héllo"
            },
            {
              "type": "message",
              "data": "你好"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "encodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.EncodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-single",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "4hello"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "a body with no separator is a one-packet payload"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-two",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "4a\u001e4b"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-handshake-then-messages",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "0{\"sid\":\"x\",\"pingInterval\":25000}\u001e40\u001e42[\"ev\",1]"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "the real first polling response: OPEN, then the Socket.IO CONNECT and an EVENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-all-types",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "0{}\u001e1\u001e2probe\u001e3probe\u001e4msg\u001e5\u001e6"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-binary-first",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "bAP8Q\u001e4hello"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-binary-empty-member",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "b\u001e4x"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "a zero-length binary member is legal"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-empty-body",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": ""
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload (ErrEmptyPacket)",
      "note": "an empty/truncated POST body must not decode as an empty batch: both must fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-separator-only",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "\u001e"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "both must fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-trailing-separator",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "4a\u001e"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "a trailing separator leaves an empty record; both must fail rather than ignore it"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-leading-separator",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "\u001e4a"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "both must fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-double-separator",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "4a\u001e\u001e4b"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "both must fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-bad-member-type",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "4a\u001e7x"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
      "note": "one bad member poisons the whole batch: both must fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "decpay-bad-member-first",
      "fn": "eio.decodePayload",
      "args": [
        {
          "encoded": "9\u001e4a"
        }
      ],
      "upstreamFn": "decodePayload",
      "goFn": "engineio.DecodePayload",
